    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.completion\n\n### Description\n\nSometimes in LSP-enabled buffers I see a `Invalid window id` error:\r\n\r\n\n\n### Neovim version\n\nNVIM v0.10.0-dev-613+gdb590e96d593\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nI don't have a root cause, but mini.completion could avoid the error by checking if a window id is valid.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nNo error.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n```\r\nError executing vim.schedule lua callback: .../pack/paqs/start/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1282: Invalid window id: 1304\r\nstack traceback:\r\n        [C]: in function 'nvim_win_close'\r\n        .../pack/paqs/start/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1282: in function 'close_action_window'\r\n        .../pack/paqs/start/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1078: in function 'show_signature_window'\r\n        .../pack/paqs/start/mini.completion/lua/mini/completion.lua:1063: in function 'handler'\r\n        /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua:2171: in function 'handler'\r\n        /usr/local/share/nvim/runtime/lua/vim/lsp.lua:1499: in function ''\r\n        vim/_editor.lua: in function <vim/_editor.lua:0>\r\n```",
